description:
Surfaced during bd:JMAP-ayoz.41.7 (maxObjectsInSet wire-up in filenode-server).

The canonical extension-server template (jmap-mail-server) places a backend.account_exists(caller, &account_id) call immediately after extract_account_id in every /set handler, returning JmapError::account_not_found() if the account is unknown. The jmap-filenode-server /set handler at crate-jmap-filenode-server/src/filenode.rs:218-237 does NOT have this check — it goes straight from extract_account_id to get_state.

Comparison:

  // jmap-mail-server/src/mailbox.rs (canonical)
  let (account_id, mut args) = extract_account_id(args)?;
  if !backend.account_exists(caller, &account_id).await
      .map_err(|e| server_fail_from_backend(&e))?
  {
      return Err(JmapError::account_not_found());
  }
  enforce_max_objects_in_set(&args, backend.max_objects_in_set(caller, &account_id))?;
  let current_state = backend.get_state::<Mailbox>(...).await?;

  // jmap-filenode-server/src/filenode.rs (divergent)
  let (account_id, mut args) = extract_account_id(args)?;
  enforce_max_objects_in_set(&args, backend.max_objects_in_set(caller, &account_id))?;
  let old_state = backend.get_state::<FileNode>(...).await?;

What goes wrong: an unknown accountId can reach backend.get_state — depending on the backend implementation, this either returns a default/empty state (silently treating an unknown account as empty) or surfaces as some non-accountNotFound error. The canonical accountNotFound failure mode is not produced.

Note: handle_filenode_copy at line 939-950 DOES have the account_exists check for both fromAccountId and accountId. The divergence is isolated to handle_filenode_set.

Fix: add the account_exists block matching the canonical pattern. Verify FileNode/copy's pattern can be reused.

Scope check:
- handle_filenode_set: missing account_exists (this bead).
- handle_filenode_get / handle_filenode_changes / handle_filenode_query / handle_filenode_query_changes: route through the generic jmap_server::handlers::handle_* foundation handlers, which have their own account-validation semantics. Out of scope here.
- handle_filenode_copy: already correct.

Workspace propagation: check whether the canonical mail-server check is also missing on any other extension-server sibling's /set handler. If yes, escalate to a small canonical-consistency sweep bead.
